# Monorepo overview

This project is a **pnpm workspaces + Turborepo** monorepo:

- `apps/web/` — React + Vite + TanStack frontend.
- `apps/server/` — Fastify API server.
- `packages/@ctl/api` — oRPC routers and the shared `AppRouter` type.
- `packages/@ctl/auth` — Better Auth configuration.
- `packages/@ctl/db` — Drizzle ORM schema and migrations.
- `packages/@ctl/env` — Typed env validation (`@ctl/env/web`, `@ctl/env/server`).
- `packages/@ctl/ui` — Shared shadcn/Radix/Tailwind UI components and global styles.
- `packages/@ctl/config` — Shared TypeScript config (`tsconfig.base.json`).

Use `@ctl/*` imports for shared packages. Use `@/*` (maps to `apps/web/src/*`) for app-local code.

# Web app folder structure (FSD)

The web app (`apps/web/src/`) follows **Feature-Sliced Design**:

- `src/shared/**` – cross-cutting code used by many domains.
- `src/features/**` – domain-oriented feature slices.
- `src/views/**` – view/container components (pages-layer composition).
- `src/routes/**` – TanStack Router file-based routes (routing and layout composition only).

## Shared

- Put shared utilities, UI primitives, stores, and cross-domain helpers in `shared`.
- If multiple features need the same helper or component, promote it into `shared` instead of duplicating it.
- If you spot the same helper implemented in 2+ places, treat it as a refactor task:
  - Consolidate into `src/shared/lib/**` (or `src/shared/ui/**` for UI) and delete duplicates.
  - Export it via the layer barrel (e.g. `src/shared/lib/index.ts`) so call sites import from `@/shared/lib`.
  - Example: `getInitials` should exist once (e.g. `src/shared/lib/get-initials.ts`) and be reused everywhere.
- Add **layer barrels** to keep imports short and stable:
  - `shared/lib/index.ts` – re-exports utilities, auth client, etc.
  - `shared/ui/index.ts` – re-exports local UI primitives (prefer `@ctl/ui` for shadcn components).
  - `shared/api/index.ts` – re-exports oRPC client and TanStack Query utils.
  - `shared/providers/index.ts` – re-exports app-wide providers.
- **Infrastructure + primitives only**:
  - `shared/api` — oRPC client and query utilities.
  - `shared/assets` — shared assets (images, icons, fonts, etc.). (e.g. `logo.png`, `icon.svg`).
  - `shared/constants` — global, cross-feature constants (roles, global flags, shared limits). (e.g. `roles.ts`, `flags.ts`).
  - `shared/hooks` — generic hooks (permissions, infinite scroll, etc.). (e.g. `use-permissions.ts`, `use-infinite-scroll.ts`).
  - `shared/lib` — utilities and non-UI helpers. (e.g. `arrays.ts`, `users.ts`).
  - `shared/middlewares` — generic auth/role/check middlewares and composition helpers. (e.g. `auth.ts`, `role.ts`, `chain.ts`).
  - `shared/providers` — app-wide React providers. (e.g. `orpc-provider.tsx`, `query-provider.tsx`).
  - `shared/ui` — local reusable UI primitives not covered by `@ctl/ui`. (e.g. `page-loader.tsx`).
  - `shared/stores` — global state management stores with Zustand. (e.g. `user.ts`, `theme.ts`).
  - `shared/types` — shared types and interfaces.

## Features (domain slices)

- Each domain lives under `src/features/<domain>/`.
- **Example domains**: `auth`, `projects`, `users`, `reports`.
- Inside a domain, use **segments**:
  - `ui/` – presentational components, e.g. `login-form.tsx`, `user-select.tsx`.
  - `lib/` – pure logic and helpers only, e.g. `constants.ts`, `utils.ts`, `validation.ts`.
  - `hooks/` – business-logic hooks, e.g. `use-user.tsx`, `use-registration.ts`.
- Create an `index.ts` in each feature to export its public surface (e.g. `src/features/auth/index.ts`).
- When adding new behavior, **extend the feature** instead of putting code directly in routes.

## Views

- Use `src/views/**` for view/container components that wire features together.
- Naming convention: `<name>-view.tsx` exporting `<Name>View`, e.g. `home-view.tsx` -> `HomeView`, `sign-in-view.tsx` -> `SignInView`.
- Prefer grouping views by domain: `src/views/<domain>/<name>-view.tsx`.
- Example: `views/auth/sign-in-view.tsx` exporting `SignInView`.
- Views should orchestrate **features** and **shared UI**, but avoid domain-specific logic inside them.
- Add barrels per domain and a root views barrel:
  - `views/auth/index.ts` – exports auth views.
  - `views/dashboard/index.ts` – exports dashboard views.
  - `views/index.ts` – re-exports all domains so routes can import from `@/views/<domain>`.

## Routes (TanStack Router)

- `src/routes/**` contains **TanStack Router file-based routes** — routing and layout composition only.
- `routeTree.gen.ts` is auto-generated by Vite; never edit it manually.
- Route files should delegate domain logic to `features` and page composition to `views`.
- Do **not** put business logic, data fetching details, or shared UI primitives directly in route files.

## Path aliases

- Use `@/*` for app-local imports (e.g. `@/features/auth/ui/login-form`).
- Use `@ctl/ui/components/<name>` for shadcn UI components from the shared package.
- Use `@ctl/env/web` for typed environment variables.
- Use `@ctl/api` for the oRPC `AppRouter` type.
